  {
   "id": "G6",
   "type": "theorem",
   "name": "\\bf Theorem 1",
   "statement": "Let the centralized data $\\overline{\\mathbf{X}} \\in\\mathbb{R}^{d\\times n}$ be $\\mathbf{X}\\mathbf{H}_n$.\n\tLet the $(k-1)$-truncated SVD of the centralized data matrix be $\\mathbf{U}_{k-1}\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_{k-1}\\mathbf{V}_{k-1}^\\top$. \n\tIf there exists $\\mathbf{S}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{(k-1)\\times k}$ and $\\mathbf{G}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{k\\times n}, \\mathbf{G}\\succeq 0, \\mathbf{G}\\mathbb{1}_k = \\mathbb{1}_n$ satisfy\n\t\\[\n\t\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_{k-1}\\mathbf{V}_{k-1}^\\top = \\mathbf{S}\\mathbf{G}^\\top.\n\t\\]\n\tThen, $\\mathbf{F}=\\mathbf{U}_{k-1}\\mathbf{S} + \\frac{1}{n}\\mathbf{X}\\mathbb{1}_n\\mathbb{1}_k^\\top$ and $\\mathbf{G}$ is a solution of Problem (1).",
